  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening organizational and productive practices of small scale business women in the departments of Sonsonante and Ahuachapn</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Associacin Agropecuaria de Mujeres Produciendo en la Tierra R.L. (AMSATI) will work with 40 women to increase their leadership, networking and advocacy skills, and business development skills. The women will launch four social enterprises in the areas of animal husbandry and agriculture, with the goal of increasing their income. AMSATI will develop a cohort of 60 trainers to strengthen the organization&apos;s capacity and reach more members. The grant will benefit 100 women directly in the municipalities of Izalco and San Francisco Menendez and another 2,188 indirectly, across the country.</narrative>
  </description>
